WEBVTT

00:12.240 --> 00:14.490
<i>It's August now.</i>

00:14.490 --> 00:17.080
<i>Today, we're going to Grandma's house.</i>

01:50.000 --> 01:54.000
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

01:54.000 --> 01:55.460
<b>That-There Park</b>

01:55.050 --> 02:00.510
<i>Episode 4 "Grandma's House"</i>

01:59.660 --> 02:00.810
Your cat?

02:00.810 --> 02:03.590
Yep, Kuro.

02:03.590 --> 02:08.430
I was hoping one of you could take 
care of him while I visit my grandma.

02:08.700 --> 02:10.800
Sorry, Nishimura-san.

02:10.800 --> 02:13.250
I won't be home then either.

02:13.250 --> 02:16.340
I'm going to visit some 
friends from my old school.

02:16.930 --> 02:18.380
I see...

02:18.750 --> 02:20.000
What about you, Hino-kun?

02:20.000 --> 02:22.860
Our place forbids pets.

02:22.860 --> 02:24.900
But we <i>did</i> get them to allow a hamster!

02:24.900 --> 02:26.790
O-Oh...

02:35.530 --> 02:36.990
C'mon!

02:36.990 --> 02:39.140
Bear with it, Kuro.

02:39.140 --> 02:40.770
We'll be there soon, okay?

02:42.630 --> 02:45.130
Make sure you take good care 
of him while we're there.

02:46.000 --> 02:48.760
Don't make any trouble for Grandma now.

02:48.760 --> 02:50.640
Yeah, I know!

02:56.860 --> 03:02.030
<b>DANGER
NO TRESPASSING</b>

03:37.770 --> 03:40.870
I'm so happy you came, Akane-chan.

03:40.870 --> 03:42.760
Grandma!

03:42.760 --> 03:45.170
You must be tired from the long ride.

03:45.170 --> 03:46.760
Nope, not at all!

03:46.760 --> 03:48.590
I missed you, Grandma!

03:49.330 --> 03:52.640
Well, aren't you a bundle of energy?

03:52.640 --> 03:54.390
It's been a while.

03:54.390 --> 03:57.000
I'm sure it was a long ride for you, too.

03:57.000 --> 03:58.750
Go and get some rest.

03:58.750 --> 04:01.220
Thank you very much.

04:01.460 --> 04:04.640
Akane-chan, you look 
adorable in those clothes.

04:05.490 --> 04:07.370
Thanks, Grandma.

04:07.370 --> 04:09.710
How's school treating you?

04:11.270 --> 04:15.950
Well, since I entered fifth grade,
 I made a new friend.

04:16.920 --> 04:20.530
I got this dress from his older sister.

04:20.530 --> 04:23.750
Oh, isn't that lovely?

04:23.750 --> 04:25.030
Y-Yeah!

04:26.090 --> 04:29.790
<i>I wonder what Takada-kun's up to right now.</i>

04:38.210 --> 04:41.840
Huh? I don't see any...

04:41.840 --> 04:44.220
I thought they were supposed 
to be around here.

04:44.220 --> 04:46.440
Hey! Don't splash me!

04:46.440 --> 04:50.450
Taiyou! Did you come all this 
way to play video games?

04:50.450 --> 04:54.610
There's a monster you can 
only get around these parts!

04:57.240 --> 04:58.850
I found it, Taiyou!

04:58.850 --> 05:01.310
Really?! Where, where?!

05:01.310 --> 05:02.460
Look, right here!

05:02.460 --> 05:03.450
C'mon, hurry!

05:03.450 --> 05:04.270
Hey, you're right!

05:04.270 --> 05:06.660
Be careful so you don't trip!

05:06.660 --> 05:08.520
Better not drop it!

05:08.520 --> 05:10.200
I know!

05:14.680 --> 05:16.150
I did it!

05:16.150 --> 05:19.700
That super-rare monster is mine!

05:19.700 --> 05:21.500
Heh!

05:23.970 --> 05:28.090
<i>I wonder what Nishimura-san's 
doing about now.</i>

05:35.510 --> 05:36.890
Hmm...

05:37.770 --> 05:40.990
This goes here... like so...

05:42.520 --> 05:45.050
D-Did I do that right?

05:45.490 --> 05:49.000
Phew! It's finished, Akane.

05:49.270 --> 05:51.060
Thanks, Dad.

05:52.690 --> 05:55.260
Sorry to keep you waiting, Kuro.

05:55.260 --> 05:56.590
Looks like your room is ready.

06:42.250 --> 06:45.480
Grandma, can I help with anything?

06:45.480 --> 06:47.400
No, no, it's fine.

06:47.400 --> 06:48.960
Just make yourself at home.

06:49.250 --> 06:50.340
Look at this.

06:50.340 --> 06:54.480
I picked it from the fields 
for you this morning.

06:54.780 --> 06:56.950
We've also got some corn on the cob.

06:56.950 --> 06:57.720
Okay!

06:59.230 --> 07:02.310
What? Yayoi-chan won't be coming today?

07:03.910 --> 07:05.520
Well, shucks.

07:06.130 --> 07:10.570
They're cousins close in age, so I was 
hoping she'd be here to play with Akane.

07:10.570 --> 07:12.740
Sorry about that.

07:13.140 --> 07:16.400
My girl's already in middle school now.

07:16.400 --> 07:20.630
She said she wants to play with her school
friends instead of visiting her grandma.

07:23.760 --> 07:27.050
<i>I see... School friends, huh?</i>

07:27.050 --> 07:33.420
<i>I guess I've been hanging out with 
Takada-kun all summer vacation, too.</i>

07:36.850 --> 07:41.150
<i>Takada-kun...
I wonder what he's up to right now.</i>

07:43.580 --> 07:44.940
<i>What am I doing?!</i>

07:44.940 --> 07:48.430
<i>I came here to see Grandma,
and I keep thinking about Takada-kun!</i>

07:50.030 --> 07:51.520
Akane-chan.

07:51.860 --> 07:54.660
What's the matter? Feeling bored?

07:55.670 --> 07:57.730
N-Not at all, Grandma!

07:57.730 --> 08:00.120
You know I love you, Grandma!

08:00.650 --> 08:02.550
Oh, don't you fret.

08:02.550 --> 08:03.870
Come on out here.

08:03.870 --> 08:06.290
Kuro-chan, you wait here.

08:06.740 --> 08:09.880
Wow! These watermelon slices are huge!

08:11.300 --> 08:14.400
Grandma, this is really tasty!

08:14.400 --> 08:16.790
I'm glad to hear it.

08:16.790 --> 08:20.180
The tomatoes and cucumbers 
have just ripened, as well,

08:20.180 --> 08:22.890
so let's go pick them together later.

08:22.890 --> 08:23.680
Yeah!

08:26.950 --> 08:29.430
You know, Akane-chan...

08:30.530 --> 08:33.090
Even if you love your grandma,

08:33.090 --> 08:37.940
there's nothing wrong with being 
bored at her house.

08:39.060 --> 08:42.960
I bet you've made some
good friends back home.

08:45.470 --> 08:46.640
<i>I get it.</i>

08:46.640 --> 08:50.960
<i>Before now, I didn't have friends 
to play with during summer vacation.</i>

08:52.120 --> 08:53.600
That's right.

08:53.600 --> 08:56.350
I've made a friend who's 
very important to me.

08:56.350 --> 08:58.180
The boy you mentioned earlier?

08:58.180 --> 08:58.970
Yeah.

08:59.390 --> 09:03.110
The next time you come visit us,
I'll introduce you to him!

09:03.110 --> 09:06.020
Oh, I can hardly wait!

09:07.860 --> 09:13.110
I see, so he was there when you 
found that kitten, as well.

09:13.110 --> 09:16.980
Yeah, he told me I was its spitting image.

09:16.980 --> 09:20.350
I reckon, seeing as you're
both downright adorable.

09:20.890 --> 09:24.580
By the way, what's the kitty's name?

09:24.580 --> 09:25.840
He's Kuro.

09:25.840 --> 09:29.150
Kuro! Say hi to Grandma!

09:30.210 --> 09:31.110
Huh?

09:32.080 --> 09:34.510
Kuro? Kuro!

09:34.950 --> 09:36.430
Kuro's gone.

09:36.870 --> 09:38.170
Dearie me.

09:38.170 --> 09:41.580
Looks like he's managed
to break out of his cage.

09:41.580 --> 09:44.650
I wonder if he's made his way outdoors...

09:44.650 --> 09:46.170
N-No way!

09:46.170 --> 09:48.760
Kuro! Kuro!

09:49.650 --> 09:50.900
What do I do?

09:50.900 --> 09:52.260
What if he goes missing?

09:52.660 --> 09:56.230
I knew I shouldn't have brought him along...

09:56.870 --> 09:58.510
Everything will be all right.

09:58.510 --> 10:00.780
Take a deep breath, Akane-chan.

10:00.780 --> 10:04.890
I should have boarded him at a pet hotel...

10:05.230 --> 10:08.150
It's all my fault for bringing him!

10:08.150 --> 10:10.810
Don't go saying that now.

10:10.810 --> 10:12.210
Let's take a look for him.

10:12.210 --> 10:13.790
Kuro!

10:13.790 --> 10:15.700
Kuro-chan!

10:15.700 --> 10:17.500
Where'd you go?!

10:17.500 --> 10:20.730
Kuro! Why, Kuro!

10:17.500 --> 10:21.720
Kuro! Come out! Kuro!

10:21.030 --> 10:22.210
What happened?

10:22.210 --> 10:25.340
The kitten's gone and run off.

10:25.340 --> 10:28.720
Maybe the cage wasn't 
assembled tightly enough.

10:28.720 --> 10:29.530
What?

10:30.190 --> 10:31.590
What?!

10:33.860 --> 10:36.740
Kuro! Kuro!

10:38.930 --> 10:41.650
It'll be all right, Akane-chan.

10:41.650 --> 10:44.420
I'm sure he'll show up when he gets hungry.

10:44.420 --> 10:45.730
B-But...

10:45.730 --> 10:47.500
Excuse me!

10:49.180 --> 10:53.040
I found this guy wandering around outside.

10:55.580 --> 10:58.160
Kuro! Thank goodness!

10:58.630 --> 11:00.120
Wait... Huh?!

11:02.850 --> 11:05.390
T-T-Takada-kun?!

11:05.390 --> 11:07.420
Ah, Nishimura-san.

11:07.420 --> 11:09.540
H-H-How?!

11:09.540 --> 11:14.500
Well, you see, I was playing nearby
when I heard someone yell out, "Kuro!"

11:14.500 --> 11:19.700
Then I found a cat by the road 
that looked like your kitty Kuro!

11:23.560 --> 11:27.030
Wh-Wh-What are you doing here,
Nishimura-san?!

11:27.680 --> 11:28.580
So slow...

11:28.580 --> 11:32.430
Why, if it isn't Taiyou! It's been a while.

11:32.430 --> 11:33.000
Huh?

11:33.000 --> 11:35.870
Hey, Grandma! How've you been?

11:35.870 --> 11:38.540
Grandma, you know him?

11:38.540 --> 11:43.670
Taiyou's the little rascal who used to live 
in the neighborhood until this past spring.

11:45.090 --> 11:48.500
<i>No way... What a coincidence!</i>

11:49.740 --> 11:51.840
Sorry, Nishimura-san.

11:52.240 --> 11:54.740
I won't be home then either.

11:54.740 --> 11:57.840
I'm going to visit some 
friends from my old school.

11:58.220 --> 12:01.760
I'd never have guessed you 
were Nishimura-san's grandma!

12:00.620 --> 12:02.120
<i>His old school is here...</i>

12:02.120 --> 12:05.620
<i>This is where he used
to live before he moved...</i>

12:06.120 --> 12:10.880
<i>At this point, it's less coincidence
 and more like...</i>

12:10.880 --> 12:15.110
What a coincidence! It's like it was fate!

12:15.760 --> 12:20.160
<i>I was too embarrassed to say it,
 but he didn't even think twice...</i>

12:23.990 --> 12:26.060
Akane, is Kuro...

12:27.790 --> 12:30.510
Oh! Huh?

12:33.170 --> 12:36.900
Mom... Who's the boy?

12:36.900 --> 12:42.130
It seems Akane has chanced upon
a school friend out here.

12:42.130 --> 12:44.490
I see. A friend...

12:45.180 --> 12:47.740
Are you sure they're just friends?

12:47.740 --> 12:52.630
I'm sure I found Kuro thanks 
to your powers, Nishimura-san!

12:52.630 --> 12:55.440
I-I don't think that's the case...

12:55.880 --> 12:57.400
But I'm so relieved.

12:57.940 --> 13:02.310
Kuro! You can't go making 
trouble for Nishimura-san!

13:03.810 --> 13:09.060
Taiyou, since you're here, why don't you 
show Akane-chan around the neighborhood?

13:09.060 --> 13:09.850
Huh?

13:10.230 --> 13:10.810
Huh?!

13:11.080 --> 13:12.300
Yeah, sure thing!

13:12.620 --> 13:14.680
Nishimura-san, where do you want to go?

13:14.680 --> 13:17.130
Rare monster locations?

13:17.130 --> 13:19.280
Or the Cat Museum?

13:19.280 --> 13:21.180
I know a secret base, too!

13:21.180 --> 13:22.310
Um...

13:22.680 --> 13:23.990
Akane-chan.

13:24.870 --> 13:27.070
You go and have fun.

13:27.070 --> 13:29.490
Make sure you're back by dinnertime.

13:29.490 --> 13:30.500
Okay.

13:30.500 --> 13:32.760
Thanks, Grandma.

13:35.390 --> 13:38.070
We're off!

13:40.670 --> 13:42.920
This way, Nishimura-san!

13:42.920 --> 13:43.820
Okay!

13:43.820 --> 13:46.340
There's a really awesome mountain!

13:46.820 --> 13:49.480
You get there by going 
through a secret tunnel!

13:49.480 --> 13:50.290
Wanna see?

13:50.290 --> 13:52.190
Yep, show me!

13:54.020 --> 13:59.020
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

14:01.790 --> 14:06.210
Wow, he took you all the way
out there yesterday?

14:06.600 --> 14:11.640
I see. So he's the boy who 
called you that one time.

14:11.640 --> 14:12.600
Yeah.

14:12.600 --> 14:14.400
It all makes sense now...

14:14.400 --> 14:21.350
Oh, also, his older sister is Yukiko-san,
the one who gave me all those cute clothes.

14:21.350 --> 14:25.070
Good morning, Nishimura-san!

14:29.630 --> 14:32.110
Good morning, Takada-kun.

14:32.110 --> 14:33.670
Good morning to you!

14:33.670 --> 14:35.180
M-Morning...

14:35.620 --> 14:37.990
Did you see that TV show last night?

14:37.990 --> 14:39.920
The one where they saw ghosts?

14:39.920 --> 14:41.490
Yeah, I saw it.

14:41.490 --> 14:42.720
It sure was scary.

14:42.720 --> 14:44.820
It was <i>super</i> scary!

14:44.820 --> 14:48.910
Oh, but I bet you could summon 
something even scarier!

14:48.910 --> 14:50.910
Th-That's not true.

14:50.910 --> 14:52.900
You totally could with your 
Grim Reaper powers!

14:52.900 --> 14:53.690
No way.

14:54.580 --> 14:55.700
Oh, my.

14:56.170 --> 14:59.670
I thought you were with Akane-chan today.

14:59.670 --> 15:00.920
Ah...

15:01.460 --> 15:04.360
We ran into Taiyou-kun 
from yesterday on the way.

15:04.860 --> 15:07.580
So I went on ahead by myself
to pay my respects and came back.

15:09.190 --> 15:10.920
That boy, huh?

15:12.200 --> 15:13.040
Wait...

15:14.200 --> 15:18.580
I wonder where he's dragged her
off to about now.

15:18.580 --> 15:20.690
Don't say such ominous things!

15:22.130 --> 15:23.980
I'm kidding around.

15:23.980 --> 15:27.130
They made fast friends
back home, didn't they?

15:27.130 --> 15:30.950
It'd be nice if they can make 
even more memories here.

15:30.950 --> 15:32.960
I-I suppose...

15:32.960 --> 15:35.390
Just the two of them, y'know?

15:38.770 --> 15:42.340
M-M-Mom!

15:46.460 --> 15:49.600
I'm sorry for making you
come with me, Takada-kun.

15:49.600 --> 15:50.570
It's cool!

15:50.570 --> 15:53.060
I dragged you all over the place yesterday,

15:53.060 --> 15:57.570
and besides, anywhere's fun
when you're there, Nishimura-san!

15:57.960 --> 16:03.560
I had no idea you've always been
coming here to pay your respects, though.

16:03.560 --> 16:05.930
Yep, every year without fail.

16:05.930 --> 16:07.530
Every year...

16:07.530 --> 16:08.620
I see.

16:08.620 --> 16:11.830
So the secret to your Grim Reaper
powers is somewhere around here...

16:11.830 --> 16:13.930
N-No, I don't think so.

16:16.630 --> 16:20.540
Right around here, you can see 
fireflies flying about at night.

16:20.540 --> 16:22.190
They look like souls!

16:22.190 --> 16:23.390
Huh.

16:25.910 --> 16:28.420
You're incredible, Nishimura-san.

16:28.770 --> 16:33.800
I couldn't even tell you how 
to get to our family grave.

16:34.230 --> 16:37.000
That's pretty normal, I'm sure.

16:37.680 --> 16:38.950
This way.

16:43.270 --> 16:49.570
<b>Nishimura Family Grave</b>

16:49.570 --> 16:51.240
There, that does it.

16:53.030 --> 16:54.830
I-It's on fire!

16:56.510 --> 16:57.980
Uh, wait!

17:00.490 --> 17:02.370
Huh? What's the big idea?

17:02.370 --> 17:06.540
You're not supposed
to blow out burning incense.

17:06.540 --> 17:10.090
So you fan it with your hand like this.

17:10.570 --> 17:11.930
Is that so?

17:12.450 --> 17:13.540
But why?

17:13.540 --> 17:17.600
I-I don't really know either...

17:17.600 --> 17:19.050
Huh.

17:34.400 --> 17:36.480
That's everything.

17:36.890 --> 17:39.140
You're amazing, Nishimura-san.

17:39.140 --> 17:41.990
You really know how to do the whole routine.

17:42.270 --> 17:47.880
You say that,
but I'm not exactly doing it properly.

17:48.140 --> 17:52.070
Like here, I'm offering jasmine 
tea instead of water.

17:52.830 --> 17:55.170
Because I hear Mom loved it.

17:55.170 --> 17:56.100
What?

17:56.940 --> 17:59.820
Ah, sorry, I forgot to tell you.

18:00.520 --> 18:03.150
I've never told anyone in our class.

18:03.730 --> 18:09.680
I lost my mom.
This is her grave I'm visiting.

18:13.480 --> 18:15.600
Y-You mean...

18:20.130 --> 18:22.400
Ah, it's fine, it's fine.

18:22.400 --> 18:25.450
It happened before I can remember.

18:26.180 --> 18:28.920
It doesn't make me sad at all anymore.

18:29.590 --> 18:31.040
I see...

18:43.590 --> 18:46.360
What was your mom like?

18:47.260 --> 18:52.800
Well, she passed away right after I was born.

18:52.800 --> 18:54.370
How do I put it...?

18:55.000 --> 18:57.730
It's like I ended up replacing her.

18:58.710 --> 19:04.370
Both my dad and grandma
tell me stories about her,

19:06.110 --> 19:10.290
so I know a lot about her.

19:11.200 --> 19:15.880
Even though I replaced her,
I still feel a connection with her.

19:17.750 --> 19:21.090
So... thank you, Takada-kun.

19:21.720 --> 19:27.960
Because of you, I was able to introduce
my mom to a friend for the first time.

19:29.190 --> 19:30.500
Thank you.

19:33.150 --> 19:34.570
A friend...

19:36.490 --> 19:39.900
<i>I lost my mom.</i>

19:41.350 --> 19:44.150
<i>It's like I ended up replacing her.</i>

19:45.240 --> 19:46.580
<i>Woo-hoo!</i>

19:46.580 --> 19:49.540
<i>Now I'm pals with the Grim Reaper!</i>

19:50.130 --> 19:52.300
<i>Nishimura-san, you're awesome!</i>

19:52.300 --> 19:53.830
<i>You're the Grim Reaper, after all!</i>

20:00.340 --> 20:02.270
<i>The Grim Reaper...</i>

20:10.220 --> 20:13.780
Hey... does this mean...

20:14.070 --> 20:15.120
What?

20:15.670 --> 20:21.820
All this time, have I been 
saying awful things to you?

20:22.500 --> 20:23.260
Huh?

20:24.300 --> 20:27.840
Wh-What are you talking about, Takada-kun?

20:30.110 --> 20:31.110
I'm...

20:32.630 --> 20:37.050
I'm... supposed to be your friend...

20:44.020 --> 20:48.120
<i>That was the first time
I'd seen Takada-kun cry.</i>

20:49.500 --> 20:50.720
Takada-kun!

20:50.720 --> 20:52.770
Calm down, Takada-kun!

20:52.770 --> 20:57.010
Y-You haven't said anything awful to me.

20:57.410 --> 21:00.680
I've never felt that way. Not once.

21:04.220 --> 21:07.680
<i>Even that wasn't enough
to stop Takada-kun's tears,</i>

21:07.680 --> 21:11.170
<i>so we walked back holding hands.</i>

21:34.500 --> 21:38.670
<i>We took the slightly longer way home.</i>

21:41.420 --> 21:44.040
<i>And we followed
the light of the streetlamps</i>

21:44.040 --> 21:45.600
<i>so we wouldn't get lost.</i>

21:46.200 --> 21:50.110
<i>So we wouldn't lose sight of our way.</i>

21:52.110 --> 21:55.960
<i>I could feel my heart beating 
wildly the entire time.</i>

21:58.850 --> 22:01.980
<i>I wonder if Takada-kun felt the same way...</i>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.050
<b>Next time...</b>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.050
<b>Call Me the Grim Reaper</b>
